  "body": "### Proposal Details\n\nHi!\n\nDo you think it could be possible to integrate [gvisor/checkescape](https://pkg.go.dev/gvisor.dev/gvisor/tools/checkescape) into the compiler or at least make it a built-in check in `go-vet`? At the moment, the tool requires to compile and disassemble a Go module before performing its analysis resulting in a very slow process (duplicate work, no cache, etc.), especially for large code bases. Integrating it into `cmd/compile` or `cmd/vet` instead would allow to enforce zero-allocation on hot paths directly into the standard Go toolchain, making it significantly faster than a standalone tool.\n\nSee related discussion: https://github.com/google/gvisor/issues/14160",
